    <li><a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/using-explain.html">Using EXPLAIN</a>: estimated and actual rows, and buffer counts. <a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/18/sql-cluster.html">CLUSTER</a>: why a PostgreSQL table does not stay in an index’s order.</li>
    <li><a href="https://dev.mysql.com/doc/refman/8.4/en/innodb-index-types.html">Clustered and Secondary Indexes</a> and <a href="https://dev.mysql.com/doc/refman/8.4/en/innodb-multi-versioning.html">InnoDB Multi-Versioning</a> in the MySQL 8.4 manual: what the clustered index holds, what secondary index records carry, and when a covering index falls back to the table. <a href="https://dev.mysql.com/doc/refman/8.4/en/innodb-physical-structure.html">Physical Structure of an InnoDB Index</a>: page fill under sequential and random inserts. <a href="https://dev.mysql.com/doc/refman/8.4/en/explain-output.html">EXPLAIN Output Format</a>: <code>type</code> and <code>Extra</code>. <a href="https://dev.mysql.com/doc/refman/8.4/en/mrr-optimization.html">Multi-Range Read</a> and <a href="https://dev.mysql.com/doc/refman/8.4/en/sys-schema-unused-indexes.html">schema_unused_indexes</a>.</li>
    <li><a href="https://www.sqlite.org/withoutrowid.html">Clustered Indexes and the WITHOUT ROWID Optimization</a>, <a href="https://www.sqlite.org/queryplanner.html">The SQLite Query Planner</a> and <a href="https://www.sqlite.org/eqp.html">EXPLAIN QUERY PLAN</a>: rowid tables, the two searches behind an index lookup, covering indexes and how plans read. <a href="https://www.sqlite.org/optoverview.html">Query Optimizer Overview</a>: skip-scan and covering indexes. <a href="https://www.sqlite.org/expridx.html">Indexes On Expressions</a> and <a href="https://www.sqlite.org/partialindex.html">Partial Indexes</a>.</li>
